    "created_at": "2026-07-20T15:37:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-20T15:37:54Z",
    "body": "Hi @marcoscaceres. It's been a while since this PR landed but I noticed an issue with the command's URI when trying to understand the usage in https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/40699.\r\n\r\nWas it intended to put the API under `/session/{session id}/window/`? The `window` path actually only covers commands related to the whole browser window. While here we seem to relate to the active browsing context's window which is totally different. So this command should actually be implemented under `/session/{session id}/consume-user-activation`.\r\n\r\nIs that something we could still do or have other implementations beside Firefox already implementations for it?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/5024100443/reactions",
